{
  "description": "The export name of the React component of each behaviour (define() name -> component), so the adapter's API stays when a heading changes. A behaviour missing here gets the PascalCase of its name; an object also gives the root element where the docs' markup does not show it (tag, classes, role), and `content` for a behaviour that writes the content of its element itself, so React renders no children there: mode 'set' (the prop's text goes in before the behaviour starts, a new one through its controller's set()), 'reinit' (a new text: destroy, write, start again), 'attribute' (the prop is that attribute) or 'none' (no children: its attributes give everything). scripts/react.mjs reads it.",
